# Week 2 — Requirements Elicitation & Candidate Requirements

## 1. Stakeholder Analysis & Elicitation Plan

### 1.1 Interview Plan: Event Organiser
Goal: Understand current manual matching pain points and notification workflows

Open questions:
How do you currently match volunteers to specific event roles?
What happens when a volunteer cancels at the last minute?
How do you check whether a volunteer has the skills or experience an activity needs?

Probing / clarifying questions:
You said matching takes a lot of time. Which part takes the longest?
What information do you need about a volunteer before assigning them to an activity that needs particular skills?

### 1.2 Interview Plan: General & Skilled Volunteers
Goal: Understand registration barriers and notification preferences

Open questions:
How do you currently find out about upcoming community events that need help?
What issues do you encounter when an event schedule changes or is cancelled?

Closed / fact-checking question:
Do you currently receive event reminders by email or messaging apps?

### 1.3 Interview Plan: Privacy / Security Officer
Goal: Understand privacy requirements and access restrictions for volunteer information

Open questions:
What personal information can event organisers access about volunteers?
In what circumstances can volunteer information be shared with other people involved in an event?
Who decides who may see information about volunteers' skills or qualifications?

### 1.4 Interview Plan: IT Support / System Administrator
Goal: Understand technical and operational constraints

Open questions:
Are there existing systems that the new system should work with?
What technical or maintenance problems should the system avoid?
Who should be responsible for managing user accounts and access permissions?

### 1.5 Stakeholders
Stakeholder | Role | Direct user? | Need or concern 

Event Organiser | Plans events and roles | Yes | Spend less time matching volunteers; know who is attending 
Volunteer | Takes part in events | Yes | Know which activities need help; hear about changes 
Volunteer with particular skills | Takes roles needing skills or experience | Yes | Be considered for suitable roles 
IT Support / Administrator | Supports the system | To be confirmed | Manage access; keep volunteer data in one place 
Privacy / Data Protection role (to be confirmed) | Protects personal data | No | Personal data shared only as needed 
Community members | Attend events | No | Events run as planned; cancellations communicated 

